# Korvane Cold Chain Sp. z o.o. — Board Pack Q3 2024
- Management accounts to 30 September 2024 (unaudited, subject to the usual close adjustments)
- Board meeting: Thursday 24 October 2024, 14:00 CET, boardroom "Bałtyk", ul. Łużycka 14, Gdynia
- Pack ref. KCC-BP-2024-Q3 — draft v4 circulated 17 Oct, final issued 22 Oct
- Presented by Priya Venkataraman-Holt, CFO
- STRICTLY CONFIDENTIAL — numbered copies, to be returned to the Board Secretary after the meeting
Notes: Agnieszka (board sec.) pls double check v4 against v3 — in v3 the capex table still carried the old RTM-3 number and I would rather not explain that live. Printed copies are numbered 1 to 9, copy 7 is for Dr Kielich as usual.

=== slide
# A word from the CEO
Dear Board, I will keep this short, which anyone who knows me will find unlikely. September was loud. Citrus came early, Fruttoria Baltica doubled their call-offs in the second week without telling anybody, and for about four days Jarek's team was basically living on the quay at Gdynia.
I walked all four depots plus Kłaipėda in the last three weeks — Hanneke gave me the Maasvlakte tour in a hi-vis that fit nobody — and what stuck with me is not the numbers, it is how calm people were. On the night of 19 September the owls moved 612 boxes through GDY-1 between 22:00 and 06:00, which is a record, and Olek only told me about it because I asked why the coffee machine was empty.
Yes, we still have the Oakhaven matter and no, I have not forgotten it. Priya will take you through the provision. Please read the risks slide properly this time.
Thank you all. Back to the numbers, which are better than we budgeted, and I say that with a superstitious knock on wood.
Notes: Marta wrote this herself on the train back from Hamburg, hence the length. Do not shorten without asking her. Dieter wanted the line about the coffee machine cut; she refused.

=== slide
# Q3 2024 at a glance
- Revenue EUR 29.5m for the quarter (Q3 2023: EUR 25.5m), +15.7% year on year; nine-month revenue EUR 84.4m
- EBITDA EUR 5.9m, margin 20.0% (Q3 2023: EUR 4.5m, 17.6%); nine-month EBITDA EUR 15.7m = 18.6% margin
- Net debt EUR 57.5m at 30.09.2024; leverage 2.74x LTM EBITDA against a covenant ceiling of 3.50x
- Headcount 327 FTE at quarter end (30 June: 321)
- Capex 9M EUR 11.8m, i.e. EUR 2.4m below the nine-month budget line of EUR 14.2m
- Oakhaven provision of EUR 0.84m (booked in Q2) left unchanged — no release, no top-up
Notes: Q3 beat the budget quarter (EUR 28.2m revenue) by about 1.3m, most of it Pharma Lanes. Do NOT describe the EBITDA margin as "record" in the minutes, Q4 2021 was higher on a tiny base and Dieter will remember.

=== slide
# Revenue by segment (EUR m)
| Segment | Q3 2024 | Q3 2023 | Change | 9M 2024 |
| Reefer Services | 15.1 | 13.6 | +11.0% | 43.6 |
| Pharma Lanes | 6.9 | 5.8 | +19.0% | 19.8 |
| Monitoring & Software | 4.8 | 3.9 | +23.1% | 13.5 |
| Yard & Trans-shipment | 2.7 | 2.2 | +22.7% | 7.5 |
| Group | 29.5 | 25.5 | +15.7% | 84.4 |
- Reefer Services growth is mostly volume: container-days up 8.4%, the rest is rate card uplift
- Pharma Lanes helped by two new HAM-2 lanes for Helvetia Pharma Logistik GmbH from 1 August
- Monitoring & Software: 41,300 active KC-Tag 4 units on the platform at 30 Sept; recurring subscriptions are 87% of segment revenue
Notes: Yard & Trans-shipment is small but the Kłaipėda yard (KLJ-5) is now contributing every month, finally. Please do not let anyone compare the Q3 2023 column with the old deck — segment boundaries were redrawn in January (monitoring revenue used to sit inside Reefer Services).

