# FY2024 outlook (EUR m)
| | FY2024 budget | FY2024 forecast | FY2023 actual |
| Revenue | 106.2 | 113.8 | 97.6 |
| EBITDA | 19.4 | 21.5 | 17.9 |
| Capex | 19.5 | 16.9 | 16.4 |
| Year-end net debt | 55.0 | 56.8 | 54.9 |
- Q4 forecast: revenue EUR 29.4m, EBITDA EUR 5.8m (19.7% margin)
- Forecast EBITDA margin for the year 18.9%
- Q4 assumes normal citrus volumes and no repeat of the September call-off spike from Fruttoria Baltica
Notes: Revenue forecast sits above the top of the range we gave investors in April (104–108m); Priya is updating the guidance in the investor note after the Board.

=== slide
# Three risks we would like the Board to look at
- 1. Reefer unit supply: Thermaglide Reefer Units BV quote a 19-week lead time and +6.5% on list price from 1 January 2025; 38 units for the 2025 peak are exposed if the order is not placed by mid-November
- 2. Oakhaven Dairy Ltd claim: customer states EUR 1.12m, we provide EUR 0.84m; Seaboard Insurance Brokers confirm a deductible of EUR 150,000; mediation is set for 20 November 2024
- 3. Labour cost step in January: Gdynia yard wage grid +6.5% and Hamburg collective agreement +4.2%, together about EUR 1.7m annualised
Notes: On risk 2 Sofia asked me to say "provision" and never "settlement" in anything that leaves the building. Risk 3 is already in budget v3, risk 1 is the only one where a Board decision changes the outcome.

=== slide
# Decisions requested today
- D1. Approve phase 2 of the RTM-3 plug racks: 120 additional points, EUR 2.35m (budget line CX-25-01), to be sourced through a three-bid tender
- D2. Authorise the CFO to sign the amendment moving the RCF maturity from 31 October 2026 to 31 October 2027; amendment fee 0.35% of the EUR 15.0m commitment, i.e. EUR 52,500
- D3. Note the FY2025 budget v3 (revenue EUR 126.4m, EBITDA EUR 24.8m) as the working basis for lender discussions; final adoption is planned for 12 December 2024
Notes: Resolution wording for D1 and D2 is in the draft minutes folder. D3 is "note", not "approve" — Dr Kielich insisted on this distinction in June.

